From: FORZA-LAUNCHER-FOR-MAC-BLACKWELL-PROJECT
Subject: [PATCH] xodus-cli: robust downloads and Xbox sign-in (MetalHorizon's 30 xodus features)

MetalHorizon, after 2.1.0. docs/XODUS-ROBUSTNESS.md lists the 50 features; these are its A, B and C, in xodus-cli and
the xodus and msixvc crates it is built with. Each answers a failure seen in MetalHorizon's logs or in the code:
panics on a cancelled Keychain (10 November) and on Xbox answering 400 (28 and 29 October), a download that asked a
silent server again forever with no pause, a full disk written to again every 30 s forever, no resume.

- A (network): a tuned HTTP client (20 s to connect, 60 s of silence in an answer, keep-alive); transient failures
  (connection, timeout, 408/425/429/5xx) retried with a doubling, jittered pause and the server's Retry-After;
  the catalog, package, XSTS and licence calls retried; opening the package retried (msixvc); every CDN mirror of the
  package used; a file's requests paced (0.5 s to 30 s) and failed after 10 minutes without a byte.
- B (download): no panic left (each step a typed error); a failed file tried 5 times on the next mirror; a journal
  of the files done (.xodus-streaming-done, per package) so an interrupted download resumes; room checked for what
  is left, and under 2 GB before the index; each file synced and its size checked before it counts; a full disk
  stops after 3 tries with no-space; SIGINT/SIGTERM stop cleanly (exit 130, resumable); `status <phase>` and
  `error <kind> <message>` lines for the app (XODUS_PROGRESS=lines).
- C (sign-in): Keychain refusals and a missing sign-in are typed errors, not panics; the device token's expiry is
  checked and it is renewed when Microsoft refuses an exchange (once, then the exchange again); device registration
  retried; a refusal checks the Mac's clock against Microsoft's Date header; the sign-in status file is written
  atomically, with network_error, keychain_denied, device_error and clock_wrong states; the exchange right after the
  sign-in retried; "not owned" said as such.
- The library keeps its old entry points (ensure_device_credentials, api::xbox::run, get_xsts_auth_header) for the
  other users of the crate, as wrappers of the new checked ones.

On top of 0007, in the tree MetalHorizon bundles xodus-cli from (work/xodus), with patch -p1.
Tests: cargo test --release --offline -p xodus-cli (17, two against a local HTTP server), -p msixvc (20, with the package
reopened after a dropped connection; the pause), -p xodus expiry.
